{
  "_doc": "Google Business Profile category names (English, US) as far as we know them. Google adds, renames and retires categories, so every suggestion goes out with confirm: true and the owner picks the exact name in the GBP category box. Suggest only categories the customer's own services support: a detailer who never mentioned tint gets no tint category. The first category in words.json is the suggested primary one. byType lists the usual primary first, then common additional ones for that kind of business; byService maps words in the customer's services to a category. plan.py suggests the type's primary, the type's other categories that a service matches, and the anyType categories a service matches (a distinct trade any shop may also offer). Words match whole words in service names only, so they name the trade itself: \"glass\" alone would make a \"Glass Coating\" an auto glass shop, \"restoration\" a \"Headlight Restoration\" a restoration shop.",
